{
  "name": "optical_half_adder",
  "description": "Optical calculator: a 1-bit half adder built from polarization optics (directed logic). Input bits are half-wave plates A and B (fast axis 0 deg = bit 0, 45 deg = bit 1, flipping H to V). PBS A sends the rail up (A=1) or right (A=0); both paths cross at the single 45-deg-mounted HWP B, then PBS 1 / PBS 0 route by B. SUM PD lights iff A XOR B, CARRY PD lights iff A AND B. Default: A=1, B=1, so the table shows 1 + 1 = 10 (CARRY lit).",
